  "_source": "Live capture from plex.tv GET /api/v2/resources?includeHttps=1 with the SFLIX owner's token, 2026-07-29. Structure and field names verbatim; every identifying value (tokens, machine ids, names, addresses, hostnames) sanitized.",
  "_why": [
    "plex-safety rule 11: any assumption about a plex.tv response shape gets a recorded fixture.",
    "The assumption this pins is `auth.owned_machine_ids()`, which decides who may sign in to an",
    "unclaimed instance and which server they may link \u2014 i.e. who may write collections and share",
    "filters to a Plex server. Getting it wrong fails OPEN onto a stranger's PMS.",
    "What the real capture proves:",
    "  1. `owned` is a genuine JSON boolean, not the string '1'/'true'. The parse compares against",
    "     (True, 1) rather than testing truthiness, because '0' and 'false' are TRUTHY in Python.",
    "  2. `provides` is a bare 'server' here, but is comma-separated in general (see the player",
    "     entry), so it is matched as a list member, never as a substring.",
    "  3. A player/client resource is `owned: true` and must NOT be treated as a linkable server.",
    "HONEST LIMIT: entries[1] (owned:false) and entries[2] (a player) are SYNTHESISED from the",
    "captured shape \u2014 this account owns its server and has none shared TO it, so the real listing",
    "has exactly one entry. Re-record if an account with an inbound share is ever available."
  ],
